<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Kia union agrees no disputes for three yrs.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Kia union agrees no disputes for three yrs.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The union and the management of South Korea's struggling Kia Group have agreed on a principle of avoiding any labour disputes for the next three years, a group spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The group's union has decided to hold off any strikes or work shutdowns in an effort to help normalise the group's business operations,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Kia Group was put under the protection of its creditor banks on July 15 after they determined Kia would default on debt payments.</p>
</text>
